+\subsection{MiLMMT-46-4B: Quantization as a Net Win}
+\label{sec:milmmt4b}
+
+A follow-up evaluation round (2026-07-09 through 2026-07-10) tested three
+further candidates. MiLMMT-46-4B (\texttt{xiaomi-research/MiLMMT-46-4B-v0.1},
+the same Gemma3-based causal-LM family as the already-deployed MiLMMT-46-1B,
+quantized to 4-bit bitsandbytes NF4) scored \MILMMTFOURBBLEU{} BLEU /
+\MILMMTFOURBCHRF{} chrF at \MILMMTFOURBCHS{}\,chars/s --- the highest quality
+of any model measured in this study, exceeding even the full-precision
+Seamless-medium's \SEAMLESSBLEU{} BLEU. VRAM peaked at \MILMMTFOURBVRAM{} of
+8{,}151\,MiB available on the test GPU (98.8\% of the card), leaving
+essentially no headroom for a concurrent process; the pipeline therefore
+deploys it opt-in only (\texttt{--model milmmt-46-4b}), keeping MiLMMT-46-1B
+(\MILMMTBLEU{} BLEU, 3.4\,GB) as the default. Qualitative verification
+against a real 90-paragraph Bengali story found no hallucination, an exact
+paragraph-count match, and correction of mistranslations present in the 1B
+model's own output (e.g., a mistranslated animal name corrected to the
+contextually correct one).
+
+This result is the direct inverse of the Hunyuan-MT-7B finding
+(Section~\ref{sec:modelselect}): there, 4-bit quantization of a 7B model lost
+more than 12 BLEU points relative to its full-precision reputation and fell
+below a 600M float16 model; here, 4-bit quantization of a 4B model beats a
+1.2B float16 specialist by 1.5 BLEU. Reading the two results together, the
+paper's Finding 3 (Section~\ref{sec:optimizations}) generalizes further than
+originally stated: quantization loss is architecture- and training-data
+dependent, not a fixed penalty predictable from parameter count or bit-width
+alone, and can be net-positive or net-negative for the same nominal
+4-bit budget depending on the specific model. It must be measured per model,
+not assumed in either direction.
+
+\subsection{sarvam-translate: A Repetition-Loop Failure Invisible to FLORES-200}
+\label{sec:sarvam}
+
+Sarvam AI's \texttt{sarvamai/sarvam-translate} (a Gemma3-4B fine-tune by
+Sarvam AI in collaboration with AI4Bharat, positioned as the de-facto
+IndicTrans3 successor, deployed in 4-bit bitsandbytes) scored \SARVAMBLEU{}
+BLEU / \SARVAMCHRF{} chrF at \SARVAMCHS{}\,chars/s using \SARVAMVRAM{} VRAM
+--- an acceptable FLORES-200 score, comparable to NLLB-600M. On the same
+real 90-paragraph story used to verify MiLMMT-46-4B, however,
+sarvam-translate degenerated into a repetition loop: 62\% of output
+paragraphs repeated filler text rather than translating the source
+paragraph. The model is rejected on this basis, despite its acceptable
+benchmark score. This is the second instance in this study (after
+Hunyuan-MT-7B, though for a different underlying reason) of a candidate
+whose FLORES-200 BLEU did not predict its behavior once deployed on
+realistic input, and the first instance in this study where the benchmark
+score itself gave no warning sign at all --- Hunyuan-MT-7B's failure was at
+least visible in its BLEU number; sarvam-translate's was not.
+
+\subsection{krutrim-translate: Below-Baseline Quality Plus Control-Tag Leakage}
+\label{sec:krutrim}
+
+Ola Krutrim's \texttt{krutrim-ai-labs/Krutrim-Translate} (a CTranslate2
+float16 distillation of IndicTrans2) scored \KRUTRIMBLEU{} BLEU /
+\KRUTRIMCHRF{} chrF at \KRUTRIMCHS{}\,chars/s using \KRUTRIMVRAM{} VRAM ---
+below even the smallest model in this study, NLLB-600M (\NLLBBLEU{} BLEU).
+This alone is sufficient grounds for rejection. A second, independent
+defect confirms the decision: on the real-story evaluation, the model's
+internal \texttt{ben\_Beng eng\_Latn} control tag (evidently a source/target
+language marker intended for internal use during distillation from
+IndicTrans2) leaked into approximately 41\% of output paragraphs, appearing
+verbatim in translated text. This indicates incomplete tokenizer/decoder
+integration in the distillation process, a defect class distinct from both
+the quantization-loss mechanism (Hunyuan-MT-7B) and the repetition-loop
+failure mode (sarvam-translate) documented above --- a reminder that
+``passes the BLEU bar'' and ``safe to deploy'' are measuring different
+things, and that a full-corpus, on-device BLEU measurement is necessary but
+not sufficient for a deployment decision.
+
